cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill in your research or writing, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Humanities Writing Companion: A Claude Skill for Voice-Preserving Humanities Academic Writing"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-17
authors:
  - alias: tizzy916
abstract: >
  A Claude Code / Claude Agent SDK skill for humanities scholars (history,
  philosophy, literature, cultural studies, art history, religious studies,
  classics) whose primary deliverable is a long-form argumentative text.
  Not a research pipeline, not a polishing tool, but an interlocutor that
  engages with arguments, concepts, and stylistic voice. Features four-layer
  critique (foundation/structure/paragraph/sentence), devil's-advocate mode
  with anti-sycophancy thresholds, deep-voice preservation ("my hand writes
  my voice"), reflexive-writing support for human-AI co-authoring research,
  discipline-specific critique dimensions, ADHD-friendly interaction design,
  and engineering-grade infrastructure (version control, systematic validation,
  AI-trace scanning scripts). Bilingual: SKILL.md and README in English
  and Chinese. Designed as a humanities-side complement to
  academic-research-skills (Imbad0202) for the empirical research pipeline.
